  "why": {
    "tokens": [
      {
        "t": "text",
        "v": "A prompt row ties a label, a dataset and two texts together. The label's description becomes the command's name. The instruction text is shown to the user beside the answer. The prompt text is what is sent to the model, with the dataset's output put where its data marker stands. The first prompt text is short on purpose: what the data is, the task, one rule and the marker."
      }
    ],
